Raise the AdaptixServer workspace floors for fixed Go modules.

The pinned upstream server still requires golang.org/x/crypto v0.48.0,
x/image v0.36.0, x/net v0.50.0, and x/text v0.34.0. Trivy (severity
CRITICAL,HIGH, ignore-unfixed) blocks the compiled adaptixserver binary on
these module lines, including CVE-2026-56854 (golang.org/x/crypto/ssh:
authentication bypass due to unforced source-address restrictions) fixed by
x/crypto v0.55.0, and CVE-2026-46603 (golang.org/x/image/vp8l: denial of
service via excessive memory allocation) fixed by x/image v0.45.0.

Updating the primary workspace module raises the versions selected by Go's
minimal version selection for the server and every extender built in the
unified Docker stage. The explicit crypto/image/net/text/sys floors were
selected with `go get golang.org/x/crypto@v0.55.0 golang.org/x/image@v0.45.0`
and match the versions the full workspace selects (net v0.57.0, sys v0.47.0,
text v0.41.0). Old go.sum entries are intentionally retained by Go 1.25.12's
minimal `go get` update rather than broadening this patch with an unrelated tidy.

